Kernel Spinlock

CAS-based spinlock for multi-core synchronization.
Wraps architecture-specific spinlock primitives.

A spinlock is a single i64 word: 0 = free, 1 = held.
Acquiring disables interrupts (after lock obtained).
Releasing re-enables interrupts (before lock released).

On single-core systems, these degrade gracefully:
the CAS always succeeds immediately, so the cost is
just the CAS instruction + cli/sti — same as before.

    module oskit.kernel

    import oskit.arch.{arch_spinlock_acquire, arch_spinlock_release}

Initialize a spinlock to the unlocked state.

    spinlock_init(lock: *i64)
        *lock = i64(0)

Acquire the spinlock. Spins until the lock is free,
then atomically claims it and disables interrupts.

    spinlock_acquire(lock: *i64)
        arch_spinlock_acquire(lock)

Release the spinlock. Re-enables interrupts and
stores 0 to the lock word.

    spinlock_release(lock: *i64)
        arch_spinlock_release(lock)
